Z||000000||GTMike||07-12-2001||02:52 PM||||well my service eng soon light came on. and i need to know what the problem is.   you guys keep talking about. " what codes is it giveing you"  so  i'm assuming you can get some hand held computer gizzmo. and pulg it in to the wireing harnes and it will tell you whats wrong. and why the light is on.<P>i have good oil presser. good temp. and supper good  gas milage.  i got 30 mpg on the way from las vages to colorado.<P>where can i get one of these engine decoder things if they exist.<BR>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||k2m4||07-12-2001||03:13 PM||||1. grab a paper clip and un bend it<BR>2. Get a t-25 torx screw driver and remove the 2 screw on the cigerette lighter face plate and you will see a small harness<BR>3. take your unfolded paper clip and ground i beleieve its pin 1 and 2 *********NOTE i may be wrong. I can tell by looking at it ...but not off the top of my head. <BR>4. turn your key on and it will spit the codes at you begining with code 12 the the bad then it finishes with code 12 <P>check the link out here:http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/codes.html<P><BR>kerm <BR>86 2M4<BR>86 1/2 GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Steve Normington||07-12-2001||03:37 PM||||The two pins are actually called A and B. They are the two pins on the top of the connector near the passenger side of the car.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||07-12-2001||03:38 PM||||Once you short the terminals (key on, motor not running) the Check Engine light will start blinking the codes. Count the blinks. It will start by blinking code 12 three times. <BR>Code 12 is normal. It's a system check.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||07-12-2001||04:00 PM||||Pick up a Haynes manual(you'll need it eventually) and it will explain the entire procedure and give you the meaning of each of the codes.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||07-12-2001||04:04 PM||||Turn the ignition switch to on...do not start the car.  The first stop when you would start the car and the idiot lights come on.  The check engine light will blink at you. *...**...*...**...*...** is code 12 which says every thing is ok<P>The next series are the trouble codes:***...**...***...**...***...** is the infamous code 32, EGR system.  It will do all the codes until it cycles back to code 12, then start over.<P>Just jot down the codes that come up.||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||07-12-2001||05:37 PM||||Aren't the screws T-15? Mine are.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierosound||07-12-2001||07:19 PM||||The troublrshooting page at this website may help.  All the CODES are also listed<BR> <A HREF="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/troubleshooting.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://fierodude.hypermart.net/troubleshooting.htm</A> <P>||||reg||1
