Z||000012||Steve Normington||07-12-2001||09:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GTMike:<BR><B>how do you know if there are no problems. <P>2 code 12s in a row??<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Four code 12's in a row means no stored codes. The ECM flashes code 12 three time, then any stored codes three times, then code 12 continuously.||||reg||1
Z||000013||terryk||07-12-2001||10:40 PM||||Actually, Code 12 is an malfunction code and doesn't mean "no codes". It means no reference pulses from the ignition. This is normal since the engine isn't running. It goes away if you jumper A and B when the car is running because it's getting pulses.<P>Excellent information for boring your friends over a beer.||||reg||1
